###  https://w3id.org/polymat/AtomicForceMicroscope
<https://w3id.org/polymat/AtomicForceMicroscope> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/polymat/Microscope> ;
                                                 rdfs:comment """A microscope which uses a sharp spike tip mounted on the end of a cantilever to scan the surface of the specimen; an image of the surface is obtained by mechanically moving the probe in a raster scan of the specimen, line by line, and recording the force experienced by the tip as a function of position; a feedback loop is used to maintain a fixed relationship between the tip and surface during scanning
(http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0000954)"""@en ,
                                                              """A scanning probe microscope that has nanometer resolution. It consists of a microscale cantilever, a laser, an array of photodiodes and a detection system
(http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C78804)"""@en ;
                                                 rdfs:label "Atomic force microscope"@en ;
                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "AFM"@en .


