:SupercriticalCO2 rdfs:comment "Carbon dioxide in supercritical state (above 31.1°C and 72.9 bar), commonly used for aerogel drying. The plain gas is modelled separately as gmat:CarbonDioxide; this class denotes the supercritical state of that substance"@en ;
                  rdfs:label "Supercritical CO2"@en ;
                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Carbon dioxide in the supercritical state, used as a low-surface-tension drying medium in supercritical drying of gels"@en ;
                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_16526> .


:TEMImaging rdfs:comment "Transmission electron microscopy imaging of the primary particle and pore network structure; performed on a pmat:TransmissionElectronMicroscope"@en ;
