                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/11636> ;
                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A chlorosilane silylating agent that converts hydrophilic surface silanols to hydrophobic trimethylsilyl groups, enabling ambient pressure drying without pore collapse"@en .


:Urea rdfs:comment "Urea (CO(NH2)2), used for in-situ base generation (thermal hydrolysis to ammonia) in one-pot MTMS/TMOS syntheses and as nitrogen source for N-doped carbon aerogels"@en ;
      rdfs:label "Urea"@en ;
      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The diamide CO(NH2)2, used for in-situ base generation and as a co-monomer in sol-gel processing"@en ;
